      "clause": "5.2",
      "title": "In all instances where",
      "text": "5.2 In all instances where the coating material has a tar or similar base, it shall be smooth and tenacious, and hard enough not to flow when exposed to a temperature of 65°C but not so brittle at a temperature of 0°C as to chip off when scribed lightly with a pensknife. For detailed information, refer to  IS 8794 : 1988. Specification for cast iron detachable joints for use with asbestos cement pressure pipes (first  revision). *Asbestos Cement Pressure Pipes (Third Revision).",
